    "english":  "The playful otters dive into the deep lotus tanks,\nfrightening the carp among the broad green leaves,\nin your fertile river-town where bells chime from swift chariots.\nYou return to our threshold at dawn, smelling of stranger\u0027s perfume,\nyour chest marked with red paste from another woman\u0027s jewels!\nDo not touch the hem of my garment with deceitful apologies;\ngo back to the courtesans whose smiles you bought with flattering words.\nMy heart is weary of your hollow vows,\nand tears no longer flow to quench your pretended remorse!",
